WEBVTT

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:05.020
Monday morning. No angry voicemails.

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.780
Riley's table went out at 53 of 54, with the one missing game named.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.210
That is what Friday taught.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.170
No errors describes only the program.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.610
A coverage record, checked against what should exist,

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.850
describes the data. And anything it can't see is unknown.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.290
Never zero.

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:31.790
Tuesday. Kick adds a tidy rule to spell out school names on the

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.640
published table. An "St." becomes State.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.400
Great for Brightwater. Less great for State Lambert.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.760
St. Lambert (voicemail): Hi, this is Saint Lambert soccer.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.250
Saint, as in the saint. Your table says State Lambert.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.080
We are not a state school.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.130
Please fix it.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.710
Kick: Fixed. Saint stays Saint.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.840
One line.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.050
The code is fixed in a minute.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.200
Friday's table isn't. Ask the eight sites again,

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.170
and you won't get Friday's standings.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.690
You'll get Tuesday's pages, with weekend updates mixed in.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.330
And Dunmore might not answer at all.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:11.500
This time, Riley knows what to ask.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.440
Riley: Can you rebuild Friday's table from the pages you kept,

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.130
without asking a single site again, and show me you did?

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.100
Module 2: The raw archive
